      {
        "id": 153545,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-01-20T04:46:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Mint on Advanced</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I, too, erroneously used Wrest the Mind on the Psi-Weaver. Since it's immune to its own attacks, it ends up hitting Visionary over and over. Dangerous, dangerous mistake!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>After that, though, it was actually a pretty easy game. The key was Dark Visionary controlling Voss' deck so that the ships and Forced Deployments didn't come out, though at one point there was no choice, as two Forced Deployments were revealed. Even then, the trash was pretty light on minions. Between Tempest slowing down the deck with Into the Stratosphere and (I think) Visionary having done one or two Suggestions, there just wasn't much in there.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Got out both Electrical Storm and Demoralization. Combined with Galvanize and Tempest's base power, that was a lot of attacks against anything Voss played, so the field stayed clean every round. Legacy also got out Motivational Charge and the Legacy Ring to keep the heroes reasonably high in HP. Ended the game with all heroes in the low teens. Used Twist the Ether to mostly neuter Voss' attacks.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So, it was a fairly lengthy game as I whittled away at Voss, but I never felt in much danger. If I remember correctly there was not just one, but two early Meteor Storms. It was an interesting decision to decide whether or not to use them, but I elected to get rid of them and focus on keeping Voss pinned down to few/no cards in play.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dark Visionary for MVP</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:32:54.134Z",
